{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:00b3e70f2d041f58","name":"Feeorin","source":{"id":"source:reference-00b3e70f2d041f58","title":"Feeorin","revision":27372,"timestamp":"2025-12-29T16:36:44Z","sha256":"0692ce34b9682cd728110c3b10cb9a2e80e72535a7c098d178a5e5e30f8b8a01","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=27372","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Feeorin&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-00b3e70f2d041f58","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["In ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic_Era"},", the Feeorin are known to come from the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Odryn"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Odryn","referenceId":"reference:59b48e97ba29b86d"},", a planet of severe climatic extremes. Little else is known about the world, given the closed nature of Feeorin society. Few Feeorin venture from their homeworld, and those few outsiders who have survived a visit there tell of a world well suited for the Feeorin, but nobody else.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Feeorin are massive humanoids whose aging process allows them to grow stronger and more powerful until they die, dropping dead suddenly of old age. Because they are long-lived, they have ample time to gather and use their strength. Feeorin who travel offworld typically select careers compatible with their self-serving and aggressive nature. Feeorin encountered on their homeworld display a greater range of personality and motivation. In either case, Feeorin do not seek out acquaintance with members of other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Feeorin Characteristics"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Personality:"]}," Feeorin are reputed to be brutal and dangerous. While this is not entirely the case, they are quick to anger and highly impersonal. They typically place their own affairs above others, causing other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," to regard them as selfish. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Physical Description:"]}," Feeorin are massive, highly muscled humanoids standing over 2 meters tall. Their skin tones vary wildly, from coal black to pale white but are more commonly green, yellow, or blue. Half-meter-long tendrils hang from the sides and backs of their head. They also have bright red eyes. A typical Feeorin stands 2.2 meters tall and weighs 125 kilograms.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Age Groups"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Age_Groups"},":"]}," Feeorin age at the following stages:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHILD\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["YOUNG ADULT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["ADULT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MIDDLE AGE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["OLD\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["VENERABLE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1-11 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["12-16 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["17-194 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["195-324 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["325-399 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["400+ Years\n"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Homeworld:"]}," The harsh Outer Rim world of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Odryn"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Odryn","referenceId":"reference:59b48e97ba29b86d"},", but this knowledge is lost by the classic era.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Feeorin speak and read their own language, also named Feeorin, as well as Basic.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Example Names:"]}," Bral, Crayl, Dod, Dreyla, Fein, Kren, Nor, Nym, Pryn, Sayla, Zun.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Adventurers:"]}," Feeorin adventurers are typically ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldiers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldiers"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrels"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrels"},". Force-users are uncommon, though rare Feeorin ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," are known to have become ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Knights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Knights"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Masters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Masters"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Feeorin Species Traits"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Feeorin share the following Species Traits:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Ability Modifiers:"]}," All Feeorin receive a +2 bonus to both their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"},", but suffer -2 penalties to their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Charisma"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Charisma"},". Feeorin are big and brawny, but tend to be blunt and short-tempered."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Medium Size:"]}," As medium creatures, Feeorin have no special bonuses or penalties due to their size."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Feeorin have a base speed of 6 squares."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Brutal:"]}," Feeorin are vicious combatants who do not hesitate to strike vulnerable areas or fight dirty. Once per encounter, after making a successful ",{"tag":"a","children":["Melee Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Melee_Attack"},", a Feeorin may treat its opponent's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"}," as though it were 5 points lower when determining the result of the attack."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Great Fortitude:"]}," Feeorin gain a +2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," bonus to their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},", accounting for their great physical condition."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Inborn Resilience:"]}," Feeorin are highly resilient to physical attack. A Feeorin can catch a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Second Wind"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Second_Wind"}," even when ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unconscious"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unconscious"}," (no Action required, but the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Second Wind"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Second_Wind"}," can only be taken when the Feeorin would normally get a turn). Catching a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Second Wind"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Second_Wind"}," while ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unconscious"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unconscious"}," also move the Feeorin +3 steps on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Low-Light Vision:"]}," Feeorin ignore ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concealment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concealment"}," from darkness (but not ",{"tag":"a","children":["Total Concealment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Total_Concealment"},")."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Stronger by Age:"]}," At Middle Age, a Feeorin adds a +1 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," bonus to all ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"}," checks. At Old, this bonus increases to +2. Feeorin do not increase their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Charisma"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Charisma"}," or decrease their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"}," as they ",{"tag":"a","children":["Age"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Age"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Automatic Languages:"]}," All Feeorin can speak, read, and write both Basic and Feeorin."]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
